.\" Leon Common Types — Man Page
.TH LEON-COMMON 7 "2026-08-02" "leon-common 0.7.0" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
leon-common \- shared firmware-geometry types and boot config parser for Leon
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B leon-common
documents the types shared between the Leon bootloader
.BR lbl ,
its EFI-stub kernel
.BR lbl-kernel ,
and the host build tool
.BR lbt :
the GOP frame buffer description, the ACPI BGRT logo metadata, and the boot
configuration file the bootloader validates at every boot.
There is no handoff blob: the kernel is a plain UEFI application that acquires
the GOP framebuffer and the BGRT itself after being chainloaded, so these types
are shared purely as a common representation. Every type is
.B repr(C)
and the crate is
.B #![no_std]
with zero dependencies.
.SH FRAMEBUFFER
.TP
.B base
Physical address of the frame buffer.
.TP
.B size
Frame buffer size in bytes.
.TP
.B width
Horizontal resolution in pixels.
.TP
.B height
Vertical resolution in pixels.
.TP
.B stride
Pixels per scan line (>= width).
.TP
.B format
One of:
.RS
.TP
.B Rgbx (0)
32-bit, red-green-blue-ignored.
.TP
.B Bgrx (1)
32-bit, blue-green-red-ignored (most common on UEFI).
.TP
.B Bitmask (2)
Custom format; color masks describe the layout.
.TP
.B BltOnly (3)
Not directly drawable; only BLT.
.RE
.SH BGRT
.TP
.B image_address
Physical address of the raw BMP logo.
.TP
.B offset_x , offset_y
Logo offset on screen.
.TP
.B image_width , image_height
Logo size in pixels.
.TP
.B status
BGRT status byte (bit 0 = DISPLAYED).
.TP
.B image_type
BGRT image type (0 = bitmap).
The helper
.B rect()
returns the on-screen bounding box
.IR (x0, y0, x1, y1) ,
where \fIx1\fR and \fIy1\fR are exclusive.
.SH BOOT CONFIG
The bootloader reads
.I \eEFI\eleon\eboot.toml
(kept on the boot volume, written by
.BR "lbc config set" )
and validates it with the shared
.B boot_config
parser. Supported keys:
.TP
.B timeout
Seconds to wait before booting the default entry (integer).
.TP
.B default_entry
Label of the entry booted when the timeout elapses (string).
.TP
.B theme
Splash theme file (string).
.TP
.B splash
Whether the splash screen is enabled (true or false).
.TP
.B entries_file
Path of the JSONC entries file written by the bootloader (string, e.g.
\fI\eEFI\eleon\eentries.jsonc\fR).
String values accept both TOML basic strings (\fB"..."\fR, with escapes) and
TOML literal strings (\fB'...'\fR, no escapes); the latter is what serde/toml
emits for backslash-heavy values. Unknown keys are ignored; a missing or
unparsable file yields all-default values, never a blocked boot. The resolved
config is recorded in
.BR bootinfo.json .
.SH BOOTINFO.JSON
The bootloader serializes the live geometry + resolved config to
\eEFI\eleon\ebootinfo.json with the fields
.BR framebuffer
.RB ( base ,
.BR size ,
.BR width ,
.BR height ,
.BR stride ,
.BR format ),
.BR bgrt
.RB ( image_address ,
.BR offset_x ,
.BR offset_y ,
.BR image_width ,
.BR image_height ,
.BR status ,
.BR image_type )
or
.BR null ,
and
.BR boot_config
.RB ( timeout ,
.BR default_entry ,
.BR theme ,
.BR splash ,
.BR entries_file ).
This is the file consumed by
.BR lbt (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lbl (1),
.BR lbt (1)
